<Slide style={{ width: '1280px', height: '720px', background: '#FFFFFF', position: 'relative', fontFamily: 'Source Han Sans, Noto Sans CJK SC, sans-serif' }}>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 0, left: 0, width: '100%', height: 60, background: '#0E3F8C' }}>
    <Text style={{ color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 22, fontWeight: 'bold', padding: '14px 60px' }}>"A game in one sentence" became a benchmark</Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 100, left: 60, width: 700, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 18 }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 20, color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>
      In 2025–26, generating a playable game from a one-sentence prompt became a standard way to demonstrate model capability.
    </Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#4A5568', lineHeight: 1.6 }}>
      Rosebud, Summer Engine, and chat-driven IDEs ship browser or desktop games from a short natural-language brief. Unity 7 will bundle a coding agent; UE 5.8 has experimental MCP. Industry surveys report broad adoption.
    </Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#4A5568', lineHeight: 1.6 }}>
      At a research university this is not just a product story. It is a teaching question: if a sentence can yield a running game, what are we asking our students to do?
    </Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 100, right: 60, width: 440, height: 360, padding: 28, background: '#F0F5FC', border: '1px solid #D6DCE5', borderRadius: 10, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 12 }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#1E4FA8', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 1 }}>SINGLE-PASS GENERATION</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 96, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#D9534F', lineHeight: 1, fontFamily: 'Source Serif Pro, Georgia, serif' }}>0</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.4 }}>
      of <span style={{ fontWeight: 'bold' }}>10,400</span> single-pass generations compiled
    </Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#4A5568', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>
      without a fix loop, on a professional engine task
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 40, height: 3, background: '#1E4FA8' }} />
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#8B97A8' }}>Source: arXiv:2607.10187 (2026)</Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 500, left: 60, right: 60, height: 70, padding: 16, background: '#1E4FA8', borderRadius: 8, flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', gap: 16 }}>
    <Box style={{ width: 4, height: 40, background: '#FFFFFF' }} />
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.4, flex: 1 }}>
      Democratization of the demo is real. The next question is what survives the demo.
    </Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 680, left: 60, right: 60, flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8B97A8' }}>Xingchen Zhang · NYU Shanghai · XJTLU 2026 · Panel 11</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#1E4FA8', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>04 / 16</Text>
  </Box>
</Slide>
